{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks","id":1518846,"title":"Suggested V5 tweaks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-26T14:28:24-07:00","id":1518846,"title":"Suggested V5 tweaks","content":"I am starting a V5 game this weekend for my group. It's my first time running the system. Any suggestions for the system? Despite my love for V20 my group really want to play V5 so I'm trying it out. I plan on bumping up the experience granted after each session. For disciplines I'm considering either letting PCs buy additional discipline levels after reaching level 5 or treating them more like buying a Werewolf gift; you can buy multiple level 1s at the cost of that level as opposed to making it a level 2. I'm on the fence between using tenets and convictions or the old Hierarchy of Sins to trigger stains for remorse rolls. The other adjustment I'm considering is a suggestion I heard in a podcast, having a failed hunger roll either increase hunger or trigger compulsions. Any suggestions on these changes or others not mentioned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T14:45:25-07:00","id":1518847,"title":"","content":"From my own experiances<br /> <br /> -ignore the oblivion stain rule<br /> -ignore compulsions altogether<br /> -if your game is heavy social ignore social combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and ignore the anti tech fluff for vampire physiology since they're laughable easy to circumvent anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> With your tenants issue, it boils down to how experienced your players down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-26-2023, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T14:52:21-07:00","id":1518848,"title":"","content":"My group and I have played Vampire off and on since the 90s so I would call us experienced. How does that affect your advice on tenets, for or against?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T15:00:46-07:00","id":1518849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1518848#post1518848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group and I have played Vampire off and on since the 90s so I would call us experienced. How does that affect your advice on tenets, for or against?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> with that level of experiance I'd feel comfortable trusting your players with tenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T01:29:07-07:00","id":1518885,"title":"","content":"Throw out the whole thing, play V20 and import the things you like from V5 - if there are any <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T02:18:02-07:00","id":1518890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1518885#post1518885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw out the whole thing, play V20 and import the things you like from V5 - if there are any <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I integrated touchstones as a background (xp cost reduction for buying back humanity or path ratings) and introduced the 2nd inq.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T05:45:00-07:00","id":1518923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1518885#post1518885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw out the whole thing, play V20 and import the things you like from V5 - if there are any <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That won't happen this time. My group wants to give V5 a legitimate chance. I will tweak some things but will overall run the system as is. Most of my V5 issues relate to the setting update and discipline/lore disconnect for elders, and lack of player support for Sabbat, Paths/Roads. But I'm really the only one super invested in VtM lore/background in my group. I do want to run Dark Ages again one day, as well as Sabbat games. Depending on the gameline state I will most likely have to homebrew some stuff between V20 and V5 then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T09:14:31-07:00","id":1519035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1518923#post1518923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That won't happen this time. My group wants to give V5 a legitimate chance. I will tweak some things but will overall run the system as is. Most of my V5 issues relate to the setting update and discipline/lore disconnect for elders, and lack of player support for Sabbat, Paths/Roads. But I'm really the only one super invested in VtM lore/background in my group. I do want to run Dark Ages again one day, as well as Sabbat games. Depending on the gameline state I will most likely have to homebrew some stuff between V20 and V5 then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to keep in mind for your chronicle v5 is very focussed on early neonate unlike and both settings and mechanics represent this your grasp of the beast is poor, your disciplines weak and your attempts to shore up your humanity are highly emotive and personal. Be mindful of this when designing your chronicles.<br /> <br /> Its good to go outside your comfort zone you'll be richer for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-28-2023, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T18:45:42-07:00","id":1519065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1519035#post1519035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something to keep in mind for your chronicle v5 is very focussed on early neonate unlike and both settings and mechanics represent this your grasp of the beast is poor, your disciplines weak and your attempts to shore up your humanity are highly emotive and personal. Be mindful of this when designing your chronicles.<br /> <br /> Its good to go outside your comfort zone you'll be richer for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've played the neonate level many times before. System changes are really the biggest change for us. While I have my issues with V5 I am looking forward to trying it out (that may be more driven by the fact my group has been on hiatus for the last year!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T05:48:17-07:00","id":1519335,"title":"","content":"Some things we've considered:<br /> <br /> -You only get Messy Criticals when Hunger reaches 3+ (this is what more recent WoD5 games have basically done anyway)<br /> -If you take a Compulsion, resolving it heals 1 superficial WP damage; everyone at the table gets another xp for RPing it, whether or not you resolve it before it wears off<br /> -You can buy any number of powers at each level at the same cost as your first power at that level<br /> -Bestial Failures only happen when you fail the roll and roll 1 on both a normal die and one Hunger die<br /> -Any roll with at least one success is a partial success, usually meaning you scraped by (you don't necessarily need to make it a kind of failure like some people suggest)<br /> -Predator Types can only give the first dot in a non-clan Discipline or the second dot in a clan Discipline. You can make your own Predator Types<br /> -No one uses Blood Surge, it seems, so to make it worthwhile we let you add your Hunger rating to the dice bonus. So if your Blood Surge is just +1 die but your Hunger is 3, you can add +4 dice. This doesn't increase the total number of Hunger Dice you roll.<br /> -Hunger Dice aren't used when you have time or there's little to no risk of Frenzy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T09:58:30-07:00","id":1519347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1519335#post1519335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things we've considered:<br /> <br /> -You only get Messy Criticals when Hunger reaches 3+ (this is what more recent WoD5 games have basically done anyway)<br /> -If you take a Compulsion, resolving it heals 1 superficial WP damage; everyone at the table gets another xp for RPing it, whether or not you resolve it before it wears off<br /> -You can buy any number of powers at each level at the same cost as your first power at that level<br /> -Bestial Failures only happen when you fail the roll and roll 1 on both a normal die and one Hunger die<br /> -Any roll with at least one success is a partial success, usually meaning you scraped by (you don't necessarily need to make it a kind of failure like some people suggest)<br /> -Predator Types can only give the first dot in a non-clan Discipline or the second dot in a clan Discipline. You can make your own Predator Types<br /> -No one uses Blood Surge, it seems, so to make it worthwhile we let you add your Hunger rating to the dice bonus. So if your Blood Surge is just +1 die but your Hunger is 3, you can add +4 dice. This doesn't increase the total number of Hunger Dice you roll.<br /> -Hunger Dice aren't used when you have time or there's little to no risk of Frenzy</div> </div> </div> </div>Some interesting ideas! Does the Bestial Faiure also only occur with Hunger 3?<br /> <br /> For the Compulsion, character X has triggered a compulsion, but characters Y and Z also earn an experience point? Just wanted to make sure I understood that one.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the suggestions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T10:31:46-07:00","id":1519350,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunger dice and rolling in general</b>: auto-resolution rules take center stage in v5 for good reason. They circumvent hunger dice and prevent complications on tasks characters should consider easy compared to their skillsets. If a player is heavily specializing, they should be rewarded for it by auto-succeeding on increasingly difficult tasks.<br /> <br /> This <i>does</i> extend to combat and action scenes: if the scene isn't climactic or otherwise plot-critical, it can and should be narrated through auto-successes especially if one or more characters have decisive advantages over their opponents. For example, if a PC on a motorcycle is being chased by a car, and that PC has a 6+ dice pool (three auto-successes), the chase scene can be auto-resolved and narrated. The PC dips into an alleyway and swerves around some dumpsters, going where the car <i>can't</i> and easily losing their tail.<br /> <br /> <b>Messy criticals and bestial failures</b>: these <i>aren't</i> botches in the conventional sense, don't play them as such. The closest comparison to another game system I have in mind, is West End Games' d6 system with its rules on wild dice, they mark a success or failure <i>with complications</i>. Keep those complications relevant to the roll, aligned to intended outcome, and in line with the tenor of the scene being run.<br /> <br /> For example, if a character is picking the locked door to an office and rolls up a bestial failure, don't just rule they jam the lock (the archetypal botch in this case). Rule their Beast gets impatient, takes over briefly, and the character smashes the lock, a window and reaches through to unlock the door, or (with Potence) straight up tears the door off its hinges. In this case you're giving them success-at-cost regardless of the roll results -- the door is in fact now open -- but they have a complication in the form of having made noise or left evidence, with which they'll need to deal.<br /> <br /> And from that...<br /> <br /> <b>Compulsions</b>: the clan ones aren't the only compulsions in the game, and the non-clan compulsions in the book are only examples. <i>Tailor the compulsion to the circumstances that caused it</i>, and <i>make it something the player can roleplay and have fun doing it</i>.<br /> <br /> In the aforementioned example, a good compulsion for that moment would be <i>paranoia</i>, that resolves when the PC that smashed the lock either deals with witnesses or makes sure there were none, and covers up the evidence they smashed the lock to the best of their ability. Or, if they had Potence and ripped the door off the hinges, a <i>dominance</i> compulsion to just <i>smash everything</i> in the office manifests as their Beast says &quot;fuck yeah, let's <i>tear </i><i>this motherfucker up</i>!&quot;. The former is inviting the player to double down on something they were likely to do anyway, and the latter is license to temporarily break character for a fun cathartic moment -- either way, if played well the character has successfully covered their tracks, and they've healed a superficial WP as rules already permit.<br /> <br /> <b>Tenets, Convictions, and Humanity</b>: Humanity isn't <i>Humanity</i>. It's a generic marker for the level of control over one's Beast that just happens to be <i>called</i> Humanity. Play up to that: it's well within players' remit to create Path analogs through careful Conviction selection. As the most common tenets revolve around not buddy-fucking or needless killing (at their most basic level), taken as a whole, careful conviction selection near-seamlessly replicates most Paths a ST worth their salt would allow a PC to have in the first place.<br /> <br /> If a player wants to create, say, a feral Gangrel with a conviction of &quot;never deny the Beast its due&quot;, then they should get stains when attempting to resist frenzy, refusing to feed when hungry, and mitigate frenzy- and feeding-related stains. They're attempting to control the Beast via regulated satiation and honing it as a survival tool, just as they would going onto previous editions' Path of the Beast.<br /> <br /> Likewise, tenets open pathways not generally available for PC's. Some former editions' paths just don't play well with others, and it tends to be an either-or proposition; it's far better to focus on a grouping of paths that <i>are</i> compatible through common causes. Under most circumstances, a Coterie of a Setite, Tremere, Harbinger, and a Malkavian probably won't work: sect boundaries aside, the Setite's going to try to corrupt the others while the Tremere hoards knowledge for the Pyramid, the Harbinger's deciding which of the other three to snack on <i>first</i>, and the Malkavian's probably too busy having chit-chats with a stop sign to care. The <i>players</i> aren't necessarily out to screw each other, it's just their paths and splat loyalties aren't compatible, and intra-coterie conflict is likely to overtake the chronicle itself.<br /> <br /> Introducing a tenet like &quot;never shun the truth&quot; suddenly makes that possible. That Setite still worships Set, that Tremere remains in the Pyramid, the Harbinger is probably secretive about their bloodline, and the Malkavian's BFF is probably still that fucking stop sign, but they're <i>all</i> out to learn Shit People Just Shouldn't Know, uncover conspiracies through occult lore, and all that other X-Files-adjacent goodness associated with such chronicles.<br /> <br /> Looking at it from that angle, hierarchies of sins don't really apply; there's not really a sliding scale of depravity, a character is either acting consistently with their ethics or they aren't. All that matters is how the character relates to the Beast and how close they are to Wassail.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblivion</b>: This is either the worst punitive measure in the game, or it barely matters. Best case you've got a 4% chance of incurring a stain (BP advantage versus a single rouse check), worst case you have a 36% chance of a single stain and a 4% chance of <i>two</i> stains (for high-level powers that invoke two rouse checks). Individual stains aren't <i>that</i> big a deal with how remorse works and that stain can still be theoretically mitigated through convictions, but it is thematic to incur stains from excessive or irresponsible Oblivion use. It's still iffy either way.<br /> <br /> It might be better to incur stains for Oblivion use, in event of messy critical or bestial failure. That's more thematic, as it links the stain to losing control over the powers the vampire is invoking rather than just being a randomized, passive, additional tax on discipline use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-01-2023, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T02:10:44-07:00","id":1519717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1519350#post1519350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> that Tremere remains in the Pyramid</div> </div> </div> </div>Has to be dedfinitely mentioned that the Tremere Vampiress or Vampire might also belong to and remain in House Goratrix or House Carna.<br /> These two groups are also definitely at the forefront of eing recognizable and representative in regard to the Tremre Kindred. There is also the Tremere Anarch option and possibility.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:05:04-07:00","id":1519769,"title":"","content":"The Oblivion stain thing is dumb, a holdover from old stories where necromancy was viewed as a special kind of evil. Which might have worked in some black and white Frankenstein movie, or game of Dungeons and Dragons, but seems badly out of place in a game where every vanilla Ventrue has two powers that violate the mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T09:39:50-07:00","id":1521596,"title":"","content":"For Oblivion we used a house rule in our game: You could turn a failed roused check into a successful one by incurring a stain. <br /> <br /> It worked pretty well to make oblivion a corrupting force that you could tap into rather than a subpar discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T09:46:06-08:00","id":1548334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518846-suggested-v5-tweaks?p=1519347#post1519347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some interesting ideas! Does the Bestial Faiure also only occur with Hunger 3?<br /> <br /> For the Compulsion, character X has triggered a compulsion, but characters Y and Z also earn an experience point? Just wanted to make sure I understood that one.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the suggestions!</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason, I missed this. Bestial Failure kicks in from Hunger 1. We ended up reserving them for a total failure (no successes) with one or more 1s on a Hunger Die, but that may be too rare for you.<br /> <br /> For xp, we gave everyone the xp if anyone RP'd their Compulsion that session (max. +1xp each). That way, everyone is encouraged to support the thematics of the Condition and it softens the blow if things get derailed.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T10:29:19-08:00","id":1548338,"title":"","content":"I like Predator Types as it gives a outline of what kind of skills and disciplines would be useful and players guide has some info on coteries and what each clan brings to the table and alternate clan weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T16:14:08-08:00","id":1548345,"title":"","content":"In order to increase PC survival beyond a couple of nights they should only take the Specialised distribution, use auto-success and take half at every single opportunity and don't make them do Rouse Rolls for waking. This should give them at least a few more weeks of unlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T18:54:28-08:00","id":1548384,"title":"","content":"My entire gaming table, made of both veterans and new blood in Vampire have been loving V5, and many of my experiences have ran counter to most of what has been said in this thread.<br /> <br /> So I won't say much. But the most expressive things have been:<br /> .Bestial Failure almost never happens, so mix the 'results' of it with Messy Criticals for more options. The difference shouldn't be great either way, both are the Beast acting out.<br /> .My players constantly use Blood Surge (with the Errata, that pumps the bonus) and re-roll with Willpower. So I keep the hunt rules in hand (remembering the Domain should matter, specially if they are out of theirs). And I think Willpower regenarting half per session is a bit too much, but if people are using it, then keep it so. <br /> .I always use the Three Turns rules for conflicts, otherwise it gets repetitive and bogged down.<br /> .Use the simplified NPC sheets, they are a breeze, for they don't need a sheet as complete as PCs.<br /> .Use the V5 official Paradox Wiki that has lists for all power, merits, flaws and predators. It really eases the search and opens options for Storytellers and players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T04:45:22-08:00","id":1548698,"title":"","content":"Your group may regret trying V5 if they are fans of the classic VTM, as V5 is honestly an entirely different game in both setting and mechanics.<br /> <br /> I'm an adamant V20 supporter and admittedly am biased, so YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}